{
 "meta": {
  "title": "Energy-Based Transformers for Symbolic Music",
  "subtitle": "Listening examples: continuation and attribute steering with an Energy-Based Transformer (EBT), compared with GPT-2 and Llama baselines.",
  "author": "Rebecca Ceccatelli",
  "repo": "https://github.com/RebeccaCeccatelli/music_EBT",
  "disclaimer": "These are selected examples. All clips come from the final evaluation runs: frozen final checkpoints, per tokenizer the same 16 validation prompts for every model and method, 256 generated tokens, temperature 0.7, top-p 0.9. Within each example every system gets the same prompt and its first sample (no per-system cherry-picking). Clips tagged PLACEHOLDER are stand-ins for outputs that don't exist yet. The aggregate results are in the thesis."
 },
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "unguided",
   "kicker": "01",
   "title": "Unguided Generation",
   "intro": "Each model gets the same short prompt (shaded) and continues it, with no control. All models are small and trained on GigaMIDI, once per tokenizer. REMI encodes music as bar/position/pitch/velocity/duration tokens; Anticipation encodes (time, duration, note) triplets. The EBT generates each token by minimising a learned energy with a few gradient steps; Llama and GPT-2 are standard next-token predictors.",
