  {
   "id": "single",
   "kicker": "02",
   "title": "Single-Attribute Control",
   "intro": "With a small regressor that predicts a musical attribute, generation can be steered toward a target without retraining. First the standard methods for autoregressive models, then the EBT, where the regressor's error is added to the energy it already minimises and the guidance strength λ sets how hard it pushes. Targets are given in standard deviations of the corpus, relative to the prompt's own unguided level.",
   "tabs": [
    {
     "label": "REMI",
     "tabs": [
